You can use a package-level allowlist entry in lavamoat to permit the package to run scripts while keeping ignore-scripts globally. The example shows adding an allowScripts entry for a specific package in package.json:

{
  "lavamoat": {
    "allowScripts": {
      "sharp": true
    }
  }
}

This demonstrates how to authorize a single package (sharp) to execute lifecycle scripts when globally ignore-scripts is set [1].

Define a custom rate limiter and apply it to your routes. In RouteServiceProvider, use RateLimiter::for() to key by the user ID or fallback to IP, then apply the limiter via throttle middleware. Example:

RateLimiter::for('custom-limit', function ($request) {
    return Limit::perMinute(5)->by($request->user()?->id ?: $request->ip());
});

Route::middleware('throttle:custom-limit')->get('/dashboard', fn () => 'Dashboard'); [1]
